    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0319" n="1153" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/379</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-25T15:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1918—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.29 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>616. For War Trade Board from Dye: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Referring to War Trade Board letter of January 26.<anchor n="1"
                                xml:id="d274-f1"/> All food supplies which arrived on steamship <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Bergensfjord</hi> consigned to firms at Bergen
                            and Christiania have been requisitioned by Norwegian Government. I do
                            not think any more export licenses should be issued until through
                            diplomatic channels it is made clear that consignees will receive goods
                            sent.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I concur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schmedeman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
